# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — the only entries here that are actually dangerous to omit.
# `.env.example` files are deliberately NOT ignored: they're documentation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Databases. Every SQLite artefact this project can produce, including the
# WAL/shared-memory sidecars, which are easy to forget and get committed as
# mysterious binary blobs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/
.vite/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Playwright
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: extension/dashboard/ is intentionally NOT ignored.
# It is the built React app, and committing it is what lets someone load the
# unpacked extension straight from a clone without installing Node at all.
# That's a deliberate trade (a build artefact in git) for a much shorter
# "try it" path — see the README's "Load the extension" section.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Trained model artefact. Not committed: it is a build output, it is
# specific to the data it was trained on, and a model fitted on simulated
# history must never be mistaken for one fitted on real students.
backend/model.json
# Archived model versions. Build artefacts, specific to the data they were
# fitted on, and a model trained on simulated history must never be
# mistaken for one trained on real students.
backend/models/

# Chrome Web Store package, produced by extension/package.sh. A build
# artefact whose contents depend on which API origin it was built for —
# committing one guarantees somebody ships the wrong backend.
#
# It builds into build/ rather than the repository root, so that a
# directory listing has exactly one thing in it that looks like an
# extension: the `extension/` folder. That is the one to load in Chrome.
build/
autonomize-extension.zip
